  ('handling-rejection-gently', 1, 'Read the rejection message once, then set your phone face down on the table for ten minutes.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 2, 'Write "They said no to this" on a sticky note, and under it write what they did not say no to: you as a whole person.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 3, 'Text one trusted friend a single honest line about the no you got, without polishing it first.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 4, 'Ask one person who turned you down whether they could share a sentence of feedback, and thank them whatever they say.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 5, 'Notice the small sting when a text goes unanswered, name it quietly to yourself, and let your shoulders drop.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 6, 'Breathe in slowly through your nose for four counts after reading a no, then let the breath out even slower.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 7, 'Name the one specific thing that was turned down, the application or the invitation, and say it aloud without adding "because I am not enough."'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 8, 'Call the friend who always makes you laugh and ask what ridiculous thing happened to them lately.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 9, 'Write one thing from your last attempt you would keep and one thing you would change, then close the notebook.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 10, 'Imagine three ordinary reasons a friend has not replied yet, like a dead phone, a busy shift or a nap.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 11, 'Name the feeling a rejection left you with in one word, like disappointed, and say it quietly to yourself.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 12, 'List three reasons a hiring manager might pass on someone that have nothing to do with that person''s worth, like budget or an internal hire.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 13, 'Accept a hug from someone you love, and let it last a few seconds longer than usual.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 14, 'Send one new application, pitch or invitation before lunch, however small it feels.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 15, 'Wait one full hour before following up on an unanswered message, and spend that hour on something you enjoy.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 16, 'Walk once around your block after hearing no, noticing three things you can see along the way.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 17, 'Picture a friend telling you about the same rejection, then text yourself the exact words you would send them.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 18, 'Ask a close friend over lunch about a rejection they lived through and what helped them feel steady again.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 19, 'Request a table by the window at a cafe today, just to practice hearing either answer calmly.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 20, 'Put your phone in another room for twenty minutes after posting something, so the likes cannot set your mood.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 21, 'Pour a full glass of water after a hard rejection email and sip it slowly before doing anything else.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 22, 'Count the yeses you can remember from the past few years, small ones included, and jot them in your phone''s notes before bed.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 23, 'Let a coworker buy you a coffee this morning and simply say thank you instead of insisting on paying.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 24, 'Open a fresh page titled "Things I tried" and add the most recent ask you made.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 25, 'Jot down one thing you liked about your post before you check how many people reacted to it.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 26, 'Eat something simple, like toast or a banana, within the first hour after a rejection lands.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 27, 'Recall a past no that cleared the way for something better, and spend two minutes writing how that turned out.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 28, 'Open the folder of kind messages you have saved and read three of them slowly before bed.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 29, 'Email a short thank you to someone who said no, saying you appreciated their time.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 30, 'Tell yourself, "A quiet room is not a verdict," after your idea gets little response in a meeting.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 31, 'Wait at least an hour before replying to a rejection, even if a reply is already forming in your head.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 32, 'Put three things about you that this rejection does not change on paper, and keep it in your wallet today.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 33, 'Send a short note to a friend who just got a no, saying you are around if they want company.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 34, 'Decide over your morning coffee whether to knock on the same door again or try a different one.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 35, 'Save your meeting idea in a notebook for another day, whatever the room said about it this time.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 36, 'Tell yourself, "This no is about one situation, not about all of me."'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 37, 'Catch one "always" or "never" in your thoughts about the rejection and rewrite it with "this time" instead.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 38, 'Sit on the porch with a neighbor on a summer evening and talk about anything but the rejection.'),
