  ('handling-rejection-gently', 261, 'Remember one past no that turned out to matter less than it first felt, and let that memory sit beside this one.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 262, 'Look at your calendar and notice all the people and plans still there, untouched by the rejection.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 263, 'Stand in the kitchen with your roommate after work and let them hear the whole story once.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 264, 'Hold a pen for two minutes and freewrite about what you might try next, with no editing.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 265, 'Cancel early if you must cancel plans, and offer a specific new time if you truly want one.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 266, 'Play one calm song after a rejection and simply listen, without scrolling, until it ends.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 267, 'Give the rejection a plain title, like "The Job I Did Not Get," so it feels like one event rather than a verdict.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 268, 'Picture the friend who would be first to defend you, then call them and tell them what happened.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 269, 'Thank yourself in writing for putting your work out there, the same way you would thank a friend.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 270, 'Practice a gentle no in the mirror: "I can''t make it, but I''m so glad you asked."'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 271, 'Fold a basket of laundry after a no, letting the plain, repetitive motion slow your thoughts.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 272, 'Jot down three things a rejection letter cannot measure about you, like your humor, your patience or your loyalty.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 273, 'Swap stories with a friend on a rainy fall evening about rejections that later mattered less than you feared.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 274, 'Wrap up your workday by sending one note to a contact who might know of other openings.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 275, 'Skip the long excuse when declining, since a simple "That won''t work for me" is respectful and clear.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 276, 'Sweep the porch or the front step after an autumn rejection, one slow stroke at a time.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 277, 'Consider that a group may say no because of size, timing or fit, and write which one seems likely here.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 278, 'Answer the phone when a caring friend calls tonight, even if you would rather be alone.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 279, 'Inquire at a bakery or market whether they offer a small sample, and enjoy practicing the question.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 280, 'Turn down an idea at work by naming one thing you liked in it before explaining your concern.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 281, 'Light a candle or turn on a lamp you like after an evening no, and sit in the soft light for a moment.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 282, 'Remember a friend who once got turned down and went on to something good, and let their story stand beside yours.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 283, 'Keep one screenshot of a loving message as your phone wallpaper for now.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 284, 'Update your attempts list after lunch, adding even the asks that felt too small to count.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 285, 'Give a coworker''s idea a real response in the meeting, even a short "Thanks, tell me more."'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 286, 'Say to yourself, "A no from this group is one door, and there are other doors."'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 287, 'Choose one all-or-nothing word in your journal about the rejection, like "ruined," and replace it with a gentler one.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 288, 'Walk to a friend''s place on a crisp winter afternoon with a small baked good, and stay for a chat.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 289, 'Circle one rejection on your list that taught you the most, and write a word beside it about why.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 290, 'Include one person who might feel left out the next time you start a group text.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 291, 'Skip searching for whoever got the role instead of you, and go do one ordinary chore.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 292, 'At the end of the workday, name one part of your job you still do well, whatever the no you heard.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 293, 'Admit to one coworker you trust that the pitch was turned down, and let them say something kind.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 294, 'Prepare a polite one line request for feedback you can reuse, keeping it easy to answer or skip.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 295, 'Spot someone standing at the edge of a conversation at a party, and turn your body to welcome them.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 296, 'Open a window after a disappointing message and take three slow breaths of fresh air.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 297, 'Ask, "Is this a no to me, or a no to this request at this time?" and answer it honestly in writing.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 298, 'Sign up with a friend for a familiar class you both enjoy, so you have a regular place to be together.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 299, 'Walk around the block after a no, and on the way back choose one next step.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 300, 'Keep it brief, kind and clear when you say no to a date, so the other person is not left guessing.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 301, 'Sort what you can still do from what was out of your hands after a no, and write down only the first list.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 302, 'While doing the dishes, remind yourself of two times someone said yes to you without you having to ask twice.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 303, 'Hold a friend''s hand or link arms on a summer stroll while you talk through the no.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 304, 'Close any rejection email by writing a brief thank you reply before you archive it.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 305, 'Decline a store survey politely, and notice that a kind no never has to feel cruel.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 306, 'Hug a pillow or a pet after a rejection and let your breathing slow down with theirs.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 307, 'Start a small yes jar: drop in one slip for a kind reply or a warm welcome you got recently.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 308, 'Gather a few friends at the beach or lake on a warm afternoon, and let the easy company do its work.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 309, 'Plan one invitation for the weekend, such as a board game night, and send it to two friends.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 310, 'Draft a short, warm reply for declining invitations so it is easy to say no without going silent.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 311, 'Stand under a warm shower after a no and let the water run over your shoulders for a few minutes.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 312, 'Imagine what a wise older relative might say about this rejection, and write it in their voice in two or three lines.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 313, 'Thank the person who said they were sorry about your rejection, and tell them it helped.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 314, 'Consider which part of your last attempt was fully in your control, and give yourself credit for it.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 315, 'Leave a kind reply on a friend''s post that seems to have gone quiet, the way you would want someone to for you.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 316, 'Give yourself one hour after a rejection before deciding anything about what comes next.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 317, 'Notice if you are comparing yourself to whoever got the yes, and remind yourself you only know a small part of their story.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 318, 'Settle into your usual seat at trivia night with friends and let the familiar teasing pull you back into the room.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 319, 'Volunteer to ask a question at a meeting or class today, as a gentle stretch for your courage.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 320, 'Check after you say no to someone that your tone matched your care for them.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 321, 'Heat up leftovers or a bowl of soup after a long day that ended in a no, and eat it sitting down.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 322, 'In the summer heat, sit in the shade and list the reasons you are still glad you tried.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 323, 'Tell your friend the specific comfort that would help, like a hug, a joke or a walk, then let them give it.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 324, 'Welcome one honest critique today by writing "thank you" first and your own thoughts second.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 325, 'Let someone''s no to your request sit without asking them to explain it.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 326, 'Shake out your hands for a few seconds after you put down the phone from a hard call that ended in a no.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 327, 'Say, "That stung, and I am still okay," the next time the rejection pops into your mind.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 328, 'Pass along a kind message you saved to a friend who just got a no, so they can borrow your encouragement.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 329, 'Request a quick chat with a mentor or friend about where else your work could go.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 330, 'Hear a friend''s "not this time" as honest information, and thank them for telling you plainly.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 331, 'Write "I asked, and that took courage" under your plain note about today''s rejection.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 332, 'Separate one turned down idea from your talent as a whole by writing "one idea" in the margin beside the feedback.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 333, 'Cook a simple soup with a friend on a cold evening, and talk about what you still want to reach for.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 334, 'Light a candle this evening and write one thing you would like to try again with fresh eyes.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 335, 'Pick one small thing you would usually say yes to only to avoid disappointing someone, and try a kind no.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 336, 'Pause at the door before rejoining your team after a meeting where you heard no, and take one slow breath.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 337, 'Mentally zoom out from the rejection to your street, your town and your year, and see how small one no looks from there.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 338, 'Ring a friend on your lunch break and ask them to tell you one thing they like about you.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 339, 'Note the size of your bravery today, not the size of the reply, in one short line in your journal.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 340, 'Look at an old photo of friends laughing together to remember that you belong somewhere.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 341, 'Lower the lights and dim your screen in the evening after a rejection, so your eyes and mind can rest.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 342, 'Think of a rejection a friend once shared with you and how little you thought less of them, then offer yourself the same view.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 343, 'Wave over a cousin at the next family gathering and quietly ask them to stay near you for a while.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 344, 'Message someone in a group you would like to join, asking how newcomers usually get involved.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 345, 'Let the sound of rain keep you company on a gray day when a call goes unreturned.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 346, 'Find a patch of sun on a spring or winter afternoon after a no and stand in it for a minute.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 347, 'Pick one sentence from the rejection message and reread it without adding meaning that is not in the words.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 348, 'Lean on a friend this spring by asking them to read your next application before you send it.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 349, 'Celebrate a recent attempt with a small ritual, like a favorite song or a slow cup of cocoa.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 350, 'Take a slow lap around your block in the snow or the heat, and leave one hurt thought at each corner.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 351, 'Whisper "Disappointed, and okay," after reading a no, letting both words be true.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 352, 'Describe yourself as you would to a new friend, and notice the rejection does not appear anywhere on the list.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 353, 'Ride the bus to see a friend across town, and use the trip to think of a question about their life.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 354, 'Write the word "next" at the top of a page and list two new places to send your work.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 355, 'Wonder, "What would I do right now if this hadn''t happened?" and go do a small piece of it.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 356, 'Chew a piece of gum or sip something warm on the train after a no, giving your body something steady to do.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 357, 'Hear "I am too much" or "I am not enough" as a feeling after a no, not a fact, and say so gently to yourself.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 358, 'Accept the compliment a friend gives you without arguing with it, and simply say thank you.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 359, 'Let one rejected piece rest overnight, then reread it and mark one line you still love.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 360, 'Return to one thing that matters to you after a small no, like a hobby, a houseplant or a good book.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 361, 'End the evening after a rejection by naming one thing you did today that had nothing to do with it.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 362, 'Before sleep, name one way you kept this rejection in proportion today, however small.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 363, 'Celebrate a friend''s recent yes with a cheerful text, even while your own no still stings.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 364, 'Smile at the fact that every no on your list means you were brave enough to ask.'),
  ('handling-rejection-gently', 365, 'Close the day by writing one line about a small rejection you handled gently today.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
